  "count_definition": "Actual executions across both SDKs, paging modes and P/E cores, not unique inputs. Focused runs are excluded. Existing instruction families have separate regression counts.",
  "undefined_flag_contract": "ShiftUndefinedFlags contains only CF/AF/OF. The executor consumes only architecturally undefined bits for the actual operation, masked count and operand width. Defined result/flag bits are computed independently. Zero masked counts preserve all flags; a nonzero full RCL/RCR carry cycle still consumes undefined OF.",
  "native_observation": "The test producer observes the undefined image with a separate host register instruction of the same count encoding. It restores host flags afterward and supplies no defined bit, KVM result, memory or exception result to the executor. The main oracle compares original protected instruction GPRs, flags, CR2, operand/stack/frame bytes and successful operand PTE A/D effects. This does not provide a portable CPU policy for undefined flags.",
  "memory_contract": "Zero counts retain writable-segment, page and alignment checks. Prepared read/modify/write plans retain native write-fault bits and original architectural restart state. Successful operand A/D effects match the CPU; the existing ordered page walker can leave a different accessed-bit image on a later permission fault, so exact faulting-walk A/D identity is not claimed. Cross-page faults publish no partial operand; original handlers repair PTEs and retry without host register repair.",
