  "retained_diagnostics": "The first native boundary matrix supplied undefined OF from a CL-form host observer for an immediate-form guest instruction. ROL AL,8 exposed different native undefined OF. The observer now executes the exact count encoding. Both the original failed log and source/binary are retained. A subsequent review also made nonzero full RCL/RCR cycles consume the explicit OF choice instead of forcing preservation; independent unit images cover both values. A broader A/D comparison exposed the existing page walker setting A before a read-only permission fault while this CPU left it clear. That raw failure is retained; the added A/D comparison explicitly covers successful translations, consistent with the existing paging contract. Production page-walk behavior was not changed or inferred from this processor.",
  "source_reference": {
    "title": "Intel SDM Volume 2 revision 093: RCL/RCR/ROL/ROR and SAL/SAR/SHL/SHR",
    "url": "https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/intel-sdm.html",
    "local_text": "/mnt/data/neverd-paged-scheduling-20261101/intel-sdm-vol2-093.txt"
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "Ordinary RAM and the existing legacy scalar/event bindings are required. Undocumented group-two /6, malformed encodings and unsupported prefixes refuse explicitly. No decoder name grants an execution contract.",
    "This adds a software protected-mode execution family, not new native LLVM or NeverC intrinsic APIs. SHLD/SHRD and unlisted scalar/state families remain separate work.",
    "LA57 is unavailable. General i386 source dispatch, real/VM86, tasks/call gates, debug producers, software SMM/enclave/AEX/EPCM and complete CET/FRED/event domains remain unqualified. Production SDK and LLVM gitlink remain unchanged; global completion and final release/pin are still open."
  ],
